    "question": "Matt did his homework for 150 minutes. He spent 30% of that time on math and 40% on science. He spent the remaining time on other subjects. How much time did Matt spend on homework in other subjects?",
    "gold": "45",
    "answer": "Matt spent on math and science 30% + 40% = 70% of the time.\nThis means he did homework from these two subjects for 70/100 * 150 minutes = <<70/100*150=105>>105 minutes.\nSo Matt spent 150 minutes - 105 minutes = <<150-105=45>>45 minutes doing homework from other subjects.\n#### 45"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much time Matt spent on homework in other subjects, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the time Matt spent on math.\n2. Calculate the time Matt spent on science.\n3. Subtract the time spent on math and science from the total time spent on homework to find the time spent on other subjects.\n\nFirst, we calculate the time spent on math. Matt spent 30% of his 150 minutes on math:\n\\[\n0.30 \\times 150 = 45 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the time spent on science. Matt spent 40% of his 150 minutes on science:\n\\[\n0.40 \\times 150 = 60 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nNow, we find the total time spent on math and science:\n\\[\n45 + 60 = 105 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we subtract the time spent on math and science from the total time spent on homework to find the time spent on other subjects:\n\\[\n150 - 105 = 45 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nThus, the time Matt spent on homework in other subjects is \\(\\boxed{45}\\).",
